run: /Users/cmatsoukis/Desktop/Apps/experiment-1/runs/bench-watchlist/wl-sort+governor@6000-03
provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist  (The request is purely a display-order concern of the watchlist page, so the sort belongs in the watchlist component (a computed derived from the store), leaving WatchlistStore's insertion order intact for other consumers (app header, search, movie-detail). No exported signature changes.)
round 1: owners watchlist=ok; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (The sorted display landed correctly (acceptance test green, tsc green), but the template rewiring broke interaction: clicking a row's checkbox or blank space no longer toggles that movie in the store. Only watchlist needs a targeted fix to its event wiring.)
round 2: owners watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist  (The owner's diagnosis is sound: the two failing tests re-query the checkbox by rendered row index, which is unsatisfiable under the required unwatched-first order (the clicked movie moves below the still-unwatched one). Their minimal edits keep the tested interactions and only locate the clicked movie's checkbox by title, so I approve exactly those two changes. Separately, the oracle error is a type error in my own acceptance test (Element lacks click), which I am fixing by re-issuing the file with a typed querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>.)
round 3: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 4: accept  (The watchlist now renders unwatched movies before watched ones (stable within groups, fully reactive, id-based interactions). Oracle is green: tsc exits 0 and all 33 tests pass, including the acceptance test that verifies the display order. The request is satisfied with no open issues.)

