        "reason": "Same conflict with the sorted display order, reported for approval. The blank-space row click DOES flip Movie 1's watched flag in the store, but the required sort then renders the now-watched Movie 1 after the still-unwatched Movie 2, so the test's index-based checkbox() lookup returns Movie 2's unchecked checkbox. expect(checkbox().checked).toBe(true) cannot pass while unwatched movies are listed first — either the flag flips (Movie 1 leaves row 0) or it doesn't (the checkbox stays unchecked), so no implementation can satisfy it together with the required sorting. Minimal change made (requesting approval): the assertion now finds the clicked movie's checkbox by title (checkboxFor('Movie 1')); the click itself and the tested behaviour (a blank-space row click toggles that row's movie) are unchanged.",
